    springsim.rigid.test.ts    5 passed
    springsim.derive.test.ts   6 passed
    springsim.grid.test.ts    10 passed
    springsim.parts.test.ts    6 passed

  FULL SUITE, one run, no splitting
    Test Files  32 passed (32)
    Tests  674 passed (674)
    Duration  105.69s
    EXIT=0

  pitch-0910.md had to take the suite in four separate runs, and every one of
  them exited 1 on an unhandled [vitest-worker]: Timeout calling "onTaskUpdate".
  This run produced none and exited 0. That is an observation, not a diagnosis:
  pitch-0910.md records the same error on base-b.log, a 28-file run that did not
  include any springsim file, so a blocked springsim worker cannot be the whole
  cause of it.

=== 7. Committed clearance, re-measured ========================================
Every committed *.simulated.gen.ts regenerated with its own header command and
diffed against the version in the tree, ignoring the producedBy/producedAt
header lines.

  vroid-sample-b.simulated.gen.ts       (mika-milfy-12.vrm)      IDENTICAL
  vrm1-twist-sample.simulated.gen.ts    (vrm1-twist-sample.vrm)  IDENTICAL
  vroid-sample-b.pink.simulated.gen.ts  (mika-pink.vrm)          2 of 10 clips
      bodyDepthMm  29.6 -> 28.1   and   48.1 -> 26.1
  vroid-studio-dressup.simulated.gen.ts (vroid-studio-dressup.vrm)  10 of 10
      bodyDepthMm  9.6 -> 16.2, 9.8 -> 24, 9.6 -> 15.9, 10 -> 16.8, 9.9 -> 16.2,
                   10 -> 16.4, 10.2 -> 16.2, 10.1 -> ...

  Nothing but bodyDepthMm moved in either file: no crown, no skirt, no coat, no
  jump. Both changed files are regenerated in this commit.

  The studio body's Body_Skin buffers 2,795 vertices and draws 2,420 of them.
  The 375 that are never drawn are real positions scattered through the body,
  x[-0.533,0.529] y[0.015,1.409] z[-0.098,0.100], reaching to y = 1.409 against
  the drawn part's 1.593: base-body geometry left under the clothing by the
  dress-up export. They were in the collision shell and standing in as its
  surface. Removing candidates from a nearest-vertex query can only increase the
  distance it returns, so a shell with phantom vertices in it reads SHALLOWER,
  which is the direction every one of those ten numbers moved.
